This lecture teaches you to create sections, subsections, paragraphs, and justifications.
Code of program.

%=======================================================
%3.Create a document to write a code to using \section{...}, %%\subsection{...}, 
%\subsubsection{...}, \paragraph{...}, \subparagraph{…} commands and using 
%environments to left justify, right justify, center, and justify text.                          
%                          Neelam Rani
%=======================================================
\documentclass [b5paper, 12pt]{article}
\begin{document}
\section{Practical: V B-MAT 507}  
This course has two components: Problem Solving and Practical using LATEX software. The following practicals of typing documents using LATEX software will be done, and records of those will be maintained in the practical notebook.
\subsection{Problem-solving Part a}  
PRACTICAL:  1\\
PRACTICAL:  2.
\subsection{problem-solving Part b: LATEX Practicals} 
The following practicals of typing documents using LATEX software will be done, and records of those will be maintained in the practical notebook. 
\subsubsection{practical 1. Create a new file in the work directory with the name note1.tex} 
\subsubsection*{practical 2.Create a document to write code for a title page.}
\section{Paragraph practice}
 \paragraph{} A paragraph is ended by one or more completely blank lines or two backslash lines. By default, paragraphs in LaTeX are fully justified, i.e., flush with both the left and right margins. If you want to typeset an unjustified paragraph, use the flushleft,  flushright or center environments.
\subparagraph{} subparagraph command starts the paragraph by leaving a space (tab).

\begin{flushleft}
This is left justified text.
\end{flushleft}

\flushleft{left justified }

\begin{flushright}
This is right justified text 
\end{flushright}
\paragraph {}Center environment

 \begin{center}
  The center environment allows you to create a paragraph consisting of lines\\ 
that is centered within the left and right margins on the current page.\\
 Each line is terminated with the string.\\
\end{center}
\center{end of practical}
\end{document}


